## Authentication (JWT)

- JWT tokens are stored in localStorage (client-side).
- Axios interceptor adds token to all requests automatically.
- Handle 401 errors by redirecting to login.
- Never rely solely on client-side permission checks; always verify on backend.

## Frontend security

- Check permissions with `canAccess(user, permission)` for UI visibility.
- Permission checks on frontend are UX only; backend must enforce.
- Handle auth errors gracefully without leaking sensitive details.

## Backend security (.NET)

- Use `[Authorize(Policy = Permissions.Xxx)]` on controllers/actions.
- Always validate user input (Data Annotations or FluentValidation).
- Use parameterized queries (EF Core handles this automatically).
- Never log passwords or tokens.
- Use BCrypt for password hashing.
- JWT tokens should have appropriate expiration.

## Security best practices

- Sanitize user inputs (Zod at frontend boundaries).
- Implement proper CORS handling.
- Use HTTPS in production.
